#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_automation_account
msgid ""
"\n"
"Automation Account\n"
"==================\n"
"\n"
"Accounting steps for ``automation``'s DAG runtime.\n"
"\n"
"* ``automation.runtime`` -- adds ``st_line_id`` (bank statement line) and\n"
"  ``diff_partner_id`` to the workflow execution context\n"
"* ``automation.runtime.line`` -- walks back through the run's incoming edges for\n"
"  the move or payment an earlier step produced. The methods are named\n"
"  ``_get_latest_*`` but return the first match in a depth-first walk, which on a\n"
"  workflow with parallel branches is not necessarily the newest one.\n"
"  ``_get_latest_document_date`` does not walk at all when the run carries a bank\n"
"  statement line: that line's date wins outright, because on a reconciliation the\n"
"  date the bank asserts is the one the entry has to carry\n"
"* ``ir.actions.server`` -- the step helpers, in two tiers (below)\n"
"* ``automation.runtime.create`` -- wizard that starts a run from a statement\n"
"  line, a partner and an amount\n"
"\n"
"Step helpers\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"A step's ``code`` reaches these through the name ``action``. They come in two\n"
"tiers plus a reader, and the distinction is the point rather than an accident:\n"
"\n"
"*Supported entry points* -- these take the run's own state and work out the rest,\n"
"and are what the live workflow steps call:\n"
"\n"
"* ``create_move_from_template(runtime_line, template)``\n"
"* ``create_payment_from_latest_move(runtime_line)``\n"
"* ``reconcile_statement_with_latest_move(runtime_line)``\n"
"* ``mark_action_done_and_continue(runtime_line)``\n"
"\n"
"*Explicit-argument variants* -- the same work with the record named outright, for\n"
"a step that has already resolved it. The ``_latest_`` wrappers delegate to these,\n"
"so they are reachable but not the first thing to reach for:\n"
"\n"
"* ``create_payment_for_move(runtime_line, move)``\n"
"* ``reconcile_statement_with_move(runtime_line, st_line, move)``\n"
"* ``create_move_from_template_name(runtime_line, template_name)`` -- resolves a\n"
"  template by name; no caller today, kept for steps that cannot hold a reference\n"
"\n"
"*Reading the run* -- for a step that needs a value off the runtime rather than a\n"
"document:\n"
"\n"
"* ``get_runtime_context_value(runtime_line, field_name, default=None)`` -- reads\n"
"  a field of the step's ``automation.runtime``, or returns ``default`` when the\n"
"  runtime has no such field; no caller today\n"
"\n"
"Journal entries come from ``account.move.template``; the CFDI use code and the\n"
"payment method are read from the step's trigger data when ``approval``,\n"
"``telegram_bot_approval`` and ``l10n_mx_edi`` happen to be installed -- none of\n"
"them is required, and the step works without them. The workflow itself is a\n"
"``automation.rule`` record and each step an ``ir.actions.server`` -- this module\n"
"adds no workflow engine of its own.\n"
msgstr ""

