#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_extract_account_bank_statement
msgid ""
"\n"
"Bank Statement Extraction\n"
"=========================\n"
"\n"
"Puts ``mixin.extract`` on ``account.bank.statement``, replacing\n"
"``account_bank_statement_extract``'s reading of a scan. Both declare\n"
"``extract_state``, so a model cannot carry the two and that module is removed in\n"
"the same change -- the fourth pair after the vendor bill, the CV and the receipt,\n"
"and the last one, which is what lets ``iap_extract`` go with it.\n"
"\n"
"What a statement says\n"
"---------------------\n"
"An opening balance, a closing balance, the period it covers and the transactions\n"
"in it. The ``bank_statement`` schema already carried all four, so nothing here\n"
"extends it.\n"
"\n"
"The closing balance goes where the model can check it\n"
"-----------------------------------------------------\n"
"``account.bank.statement`` already reconciles: ``balance_end`` is computed as\n"
"``balance_start + sum(posted lines)`` and ``is_complete`` compares it against\n"
"``balance_end_real``, the ending balance the statement itself declares. The\n"
"replaced module wrote the read closing balance to ``balance_end`` -- the computed\n"
"side -- so the comparison was against a value the extraction had just overwritten\n"
"and could not fail. Writing it to ``balance_end_real`` instead makes the model's\n"
"own check the consistency rule for the extraction, at no cost: a scan whose\n"
"transactions do not add up to its printed closing balance now says so on the form.\n"
"\n"
"Only into emptiness\n"
"-------------------\n"
"The mixin's rule is unchanged: a field a person has filled is left alone, and\n"
"``_extract_target`` is what records the correction when they change one back.\n"
"Lines are created only when the statement has none, because a statement that\n"
"already has transactions is not one waiting to be read.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_approval
msgid ""
"\n"
"Base Approval\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"Approval requests with configurable categories, multi-level approvers,\n"
"delegation and escalation.\n"
"\n"
"Models\n"
"------\n"
"* ``approval.request`` / ``approval.approver`` -- the request and its approvers\n"
"* ``approval.category`` / ``approval.category.approver`` -- request types and\n"
"  their default approvers\n"
"* ``approval.rule`` / ``mixin.approval.threshold`` -- routing by amount,\n"
"  quantity, date range or priority; adding or replacing approvers\n"
"* ``mixin.approval`` -- puts the workflow on any model\n"
"* ``approval.document.requirement`` -- documents a category demands\n"
"* ``approval.template`` -- reusable request presets\n"
"* ``approval.delegate.wizard`` / ``approval.decision.wizard`` /\n"
"  ``approval.refusal.reason`` -- delegation, decisions, refusal reasons\n"
"\n"
"A request creates an activity for each approver. Delegation reassigns those\n"
"activities to a substitute for a dated window; escalation reminds by priority.\n"
msgstr ""

