#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_conversation_telegram
msgid ""
"\n"
"Conversations - Telegram approvals\n"
"==================================\n"
"\n"
"When a conversation is analyzed, its responsible receives on Telegram the\n"
"summary and one row of buttons per proposed action. Pressing a button runs the\n"
"same approval as the Odoo form, with the same rights and the same audit trail.\n"
"Nothing new is decided here: the bot is only another place to press Approve.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_conversation_voiceprint
msgid ""
"\n"
"Conversations: Voiceprints\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"Each employee records one short phrase, once, with consent. The server turns it\n"
"into a speaker embedding (a vector; the sample audio is discarded) stored on\n"
"``conversation.voiceprint``. When a conversation is transcribed, every detected\n"
"voice is embedded the same way and compared against the company's voiceprints:\n"
"a clear match assigns the voice to that employee before the analyst runs, an\n"
"unclear one leaves the voice anonymous for the analyst to resolve by context.\n"
"\n"
"Only members of the organisation are enrolled. Customers and suppliers are never\n"
"identified by voice; they come from the phone number or the calendar.\n"
"\n"
"Runs on CPU with ``av`` (decoding), ``sherpa-onnx`` and a WeSpeaker ONNX model\n"
"placed under ``<data_dir>/models``; nothing leaves the server. The module\n"
"installs without the libraries or the model and simply leaves voices anonymous\n"
"until they are present (``requirements.txt`` pins the two packages).\n"
msgstr ""

