"but the technical scope covers any user with portal access rights.\n"
"\n"
"The module deliberately does not depend on website-editing or theming\n"
"capabilities so portal pages can be rendered without the ``website`` module.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_agronomic_docs
msgid ""
"\n"
"Product Agronomic Documents\n"
"===========================\n"
"\n"
"Author, manage and print the commercial / agronomic product documents that\n"
"accompany the safety data sheet:\n"
"\n"
"* the **pesticide label** (\"etiqueta\") — the die-cut container label mandated by\n"
"  COFEPRIS / NOM-232 (Mexico) or the EPA-style label (US);\n"
"* the **technical data sheet** (\"ficha técnica\") — the agronomic/marketing sheet;\n"
"* the shared **crop / pest / dose recommendation** table reused by both.\n"
"\n"
"Branding, theme resolution, report language and the draft/publish lifecycle are\n"
"shared with the safety data sheet through ``mixin.product.document``, so this\n"
"module depends on ``product_msds``.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_asset_maintenance_mrp
msgid ""
"\n"
"Product Asset Maintenance / Manufacturing Bridge\n"
"================================================\n"
"\n"
"View glue between ``product_asset_maintenance`` and ``mrp``: adds the\n"
"Maintenance submenu (machines & tools, plans, requests) under the Manufacturing\n"
"app's root menu.\n"
"\n"
"Split out of ``product_asset_maintenance`` because that module does not\n"
"otherwise depend on ``mrp``, so asset maintenance works without the\n"
"Manufacturing app. Auto-installs where both are present.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_msds_compliance
msgid ""
"\n"
"Product Documents Compliance\n"
"============================\n"
"\n"
"Bridge between the product document authoring apps and the Documents compliance\n"
"tracking, so a published safety data sheet, pesticide label or technical data\n"
"sheet is a tracked document rather than an untracked PDF.\n"
"\n"
"Publishing stamps the generated document with its ``document.type``, the issue\n"
"date and the expiry derived from the type's validity period, which is what puts\n"
"it inside ``documents_compliance``'s expiration, notification and renewal\n"
"machinery. Without this bridge the PDFs are filed correctly but expire silently.\n"
"\n"
"The validity periods are the document types' defaults and are meant to be edited\n"
"per company: an SDS is commonly reviewed every three years, a registered label\n"
"follows its registration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_mrp_plm
